  "details": "As a Group Moderator I have had to kick multiple people. Sometimes I am surrounded by people and tracking doesn't want to cooperate. Which has lead to me accidentally kicking the wrong person and believing the kick did not go through. When kicking someone from an instance on the Kick User Menu it does not state which user you are kicking. It only states \"Are you sure you want to kick this user?\" Instead of \"this user\" I would like to see the user's username. I am aware that a bubble appears around the user that you are going to kick. However, in haste of having to do multiple kicks, my focus is usually in the menu, and having the username instead of \"this user\" will make it easier to ensure you are kicking the correct person.",
